body:
In the parallel execution mode, there's a race condition where `this.runner.updateContext()` is called synchronously for each record before awaiting the promises. This means all promises will share the context state from the last record in the array, not their intended record context.

Consider creating a separate ActionRunner instance for each parallel execution, or pass the context directly to the execute call if supported. For example:

```typescript
const promises = records.map(record => {
  const contextOverride = { record, selectedRecords: records };
  // Create a temporary runner with this context
  const tempRunner = new ActionRunner({ ...this.runner.getContext(), ...contextOverride });
  return tempRunner.execute(registered.action);
});
```

This ensures each parallel execution has its own isolated context.
```suggestion
      // Capture the base context once and create an isolated runner per record
      const baseContext = this.runner.getContext();
      const promises = records.map(record => {
        const contextOverride = { record, selectedRecords: records };
        const tempRunner = new ActionRunner({ ...baseContext, ...contextOverride });
        return tempRunner.execute(registered.action);
```
